{"pin":"BH02848","subcodes":[{"code":"BH02848","anchor":"","first_line":"Then call thou to mind Muhammad, whose first syllable of his name is joined with the name of his Lord, the Almighty, the All-Glorious [3.5s]... ...I give praise to Thee, O my God, that the fragrance of Thy loving-kindness hath enraptured me… If it be Thy pleasure, make me to grow as a tender herb","first_line_orig":"ثم اذکر محمدا الذی اتصل الرکن الاول من اسمه باسم ربه العزیز العظیم... یا الهی لک الحمد بما اخذنی عرف عنایتک و قلّبتنی نفحات رحمتک  ","language":"Ara","word_count":"310","full_text_parts":["O my God and my Master!  I am Thy servant and the son of Thy servant. I have risen from my couch at this dawntide when the Daystar of Thy oneness hath shone forth from the Dayspring of Thy will, and hath shed its radiance upon the whole world, according to what had been ordained in the Books of Thy Decree.\nPraise be unto Thee, O my God, that we have wakened to the splendors of the light of Thy knowledge.  Send down, then, upon us, O my Lord, what will enable us to dispense with anyone but Thee, and will rid us of all attachment to aught except Thyself.  Write down, moreover, for me, and for such as are dear to me, and for my kindred, man and woman alike, the good of this world and the world to come.  Keep us safe, then, through Thine unfailing protection, O Thou the Beloved of the entire creation and the Desire of the whole universe, from","them whom Thou hast made to be the manifestations of the Evil Whisperer, who whisper in men's breasts.  Potent art Thou to do Thy pleasure.  Thou art, verily, the Almighty, the Help in Peril, the Self-Subsisting.\nBless Thou, O Lord my God, Him Whom Thou hast set over Thy most excellent Titles, and through Whom Thou hast divided between the godly and the wicked, and graciously aid us to do what Thou lovest and desirest.  Bless Thou, moreover, O my God, them Who are Thy Words and Thy Letters, and them who have set their faces towards Thee, and turned unto Thy face, and hearkened to Thy Call.\nThou art, truly, the Lord and King of all men, and art potent over all things."],"translations":[{"language":"tvl","lang_name":"Tuvalu"},{"language":"ja","lang_name":"Japanese"},{"language":"ro","lang_name":"Romanian"},{"language":"es","lang_name":"Spanish"},{"language":"en","lang_name":"English"},{"language":"zh-Hant","lang_name":"Traditional Chinese"},{"language":"uk","lang_name":"Ukrainian"},{"language":"fa","lang_name":"Persian"},{"language":"el","lang_name":"Greek"}],"writing_refs":[{"type":"pm","type_name":"Prayers \u0026 Meditations","language":"ja","lang_name":"Japanese"},{"type":"pm","type_name":"Prayers \u0026 Meditations","language":"de","lang_name":"German"},{"type":"pm","type_name":"Prayers \u0026 Meditations","language":"zh-Hant","lang_name":"Traditional Chinese"},{"type":"pm","type_name":"Prayers \u0026 Meditations","language":"pt","lang_name":"Portuguese"},{"type":"pm","type_name":"Prayers \u0026 Meditations","language":"ro","lang_name":"Romanian"},{"type":"pm","type_name":"Prayers \u0026 Meditations","language":"uk","lang_name":"Ukrainian"},{"type":"pm","type_name":"Prayers \u0026 Meditations","language":"fa","lang_name":"Persian"},{"type":"pm","type_name":"Prayers \u0026 Meditations","language":"el","lang_name":"Greek"},{"type":"pm","type_name":"Prayers \u0026 Meditations","language":"en","lang_name":"English"},{"type":"pm","type_name":"Prayers \u0026 Meditations","language":"es","lang_name":"Spanish"},{"type":"pm","type_name":"Prayers \u0026 Meditations","language":"ar","lang_name":"Arabic"},{"type":"pm","type_name":"Prayers \u0026 Meditations","language":"orig","lang_name":"Original"},{"type":"pm","type_name":"Prayers \u0026 Meditations","language":"tvl","lang_name":"Tuvalu"},{"type":"pm","type_name":"Prayers \u0026 Meditations","language":"it","lang_name":"Italian"}],"refs":[{"kind":"manuscript","code":"INBA51:042b","source":"INBA51","locator":"042b","url":"https://afnanlibrary.org/d/inba_v051/?page=45"},{"kind":